message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Congruent dissections of a triangle: prime counts, the counts up to 200, and a family of isosceles targets"
version: "4.0"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23400433"
authors:
  - family-names: Bonfioli
    given-names: Vico
abstract: >-
  Erdős Problem 634: for which N can a triangle be cut into N congruent triangles. The problem is not solved.
  Lean 4 formalization and papers on the prime case, the counts up to 200, the base-beta family and a census
  of tile counts. Not refereed; not audited outside the project. Version 4.0 adds a band theorem
  (Lean, internal audit) and a census update.
keywords:
  - Erdős problem 634
  - triangle tiling
  - congruent triangles
  - Lean 4
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ElVec1o/erdos634_primes_and_N200"
